I prefer using B!oFH or B!oEH for the HP boost myself... Much more
reliable method.
As for holy water, once i have found a co-aligned altar (or made one)
i never need to pray for holy water again. In one of my games, at one
point, I had over 30 potions of holy water... I had to be 100% sure
there was nothing around whenever I wanted to bless something, because
each time i took them out of my BoH they put me from just under
burdened... to stressed. Using this method, once stuff is priceIDd
etc, i have no problems BUCtesting stuff on myself. Not the smartest
of ideas, but safe enough in the mid-game when there's nothing about,
especially if you have the right set of intrinsics and a =3DoFA...whats
the worst that can happen? (I don't do it with amulets...so no
strangulation thank you very much)
As for spellbooks...I generally play valk, so they're not much use to
me... If not valk, I like monks, and occasionaly the odd
priest...Spellbooks are a little more useful there, but not vital, as
long as you have healing, EH, sleep, prot etc.
I'll play the odd elvish wiz, but never really altar camp for
books...Just...if i find them, wahey! More than once i've found an
uncursed book early game, read it, and  BAM!!! DYWYPI?! (damn lvl 7
spells >.>)

Getting crowned still isn't in my list of "i must do this!!!!",
however, some people seem to think it's the end of the world!
Personally, i think it's a nice way to gain the last couple of res's
you're missing. And if you do it late enough (i.e just before entering
gehe) there are pretty much no negative effects...and you get a cool
title :p

Maybe once i've actually managed to ascend, i may view it differently.
I can't say what endgame is like, seeing as I have only ever made it
there in wiz mode. But for now, crowning remains one of those things
that isn't AIMED for, it's still nice enough when it happens


